+# Selected mobile audit fixes — 2026-10-26
+
+Implemented the owner-requested **MA13, MA04, MA05, MA06, MA07, MA08 and MA10** from the [original audit](COMPREHENSIVE_MOBILE_AUDIT_2026_10_26.md). The original audit and its failures remain historical evidence. Other findings, including transport policy and shipping Billing integration, remain outside this change.
+
+| Finding | Result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| MA13 startup | Account and Race no longer await Garage construction. Production Garage retains one live showroom and seven photographs generated from the original native models, rather than seven additional workshop worlds. | Fresh graphical ready samples approximately **160–163 ms**, versus the audit's 25,750 ms attribution sample. Retained Garage **24 → 3 SubViewports**. |
+| MA04 reflections | Vinyl rotation refreshes the room reflection while leaving the unchanged car-only reflection idle. Camera, car, wash, paint, parts and visibility changes still refresh the appropriate captures. | **24 room / 0 car-only** requests over 24 playing-vinyl frames. Native reflection test detects 15,372 changed pedestal pixels and 22,475 floor pixels when reflections are disabled. |
+| MA05 recordings | One integer retains all quantized input channels. New versioned local journals store input count, proof, ghost and rewind receipts without serializing unused control arrays. Existing journals remain readable. | Actual 216,000-input append probe **43,753,760 → 7,467,032 B** retained memory, approximately 82.9% less. Exact control decoding, cap/overflow and durable retry tests pass. These measurements exclude other race memory. |
+| MA06 lifetime | Content fitting is a method owned by its button. Deferred work disappears when the button is destroyed. The same unsafe Settings sidebar pattern is corrected. | Immediate destruction of 32 actual pause menus, existing label-fit assertions and full tutorial/App flows pass without the freed-capture error. |
+| MA07 Store | Dense landscape spacing, responsive fonts and checkout grouping recover room for the five existing offers and gift actions. | Original six failures retained; **131 headless / 144 Compatibility / 144 desktop Mobile assertions pass**, including fit, target sizes, scrolling and drag-release purchase suppression. Real checkout remains unavailable. |
+| MA08 catalogues | Current visible messages are authored in all eleven non-English locales. Protocol fragments, engine class selectors and canonical creator metadata are excluded from extraction. Existing nonempty translations are preserved. | **2,620 messages / 12 approved locales**, strict source/placeholder gate passes; 13 Python localization tests, seven authoring tests and 302 packaged translation checks pass. |
+| MA10 diagnosis | Guests can explicitly copy a bounded local report from Settings > Help. Backend errors have safe first-party source locations. Future geometry builds retain separate symbols and a binary/build/source mapping. | Redaction/native-protobuf fixtures, Android API compilation, actual clipboard action and symbol address-to-source resolution pass. No telemetry consent is changed and reports are not automatically uploaded. |
+
+Cold first entry into the full live Garage remains material: approximately **12.55–14.25 s in Compatibility and 8.31 s in desktop Mobile**, including covered preparation and settling in these fresh-profile probes. Startup is independent of that work, subsequent Garage navigation retains the original main world, and a custom thumbnail miss uses at most one temporary native showroom. These are desktop development measurements; they are not phone performance claims.
+
+## Runtime and compatibility details
+
+`CarShowroom` retains its full model, lighting, interaction and main Garage Parts preview. Factory carousel images are 2048 × 512 native renders. A changed paint, kit or condition clears the stale picture immediately. The account-owned cache keys exact appearance and build identity, stores at most 14 completed PNGs, rejects oversized/invalid cached files, and releases its temporary renderer after capture. A queued finish superseded before rendering cannot publish an old image. An account change releases the old page, and navigation can cancel an obsolete first-entry preparation.
+
+The packaged preview manifest records presentation/vehicle sources and car resource hashes. It excludes unrelated menu icons and layout scripts, and the bake rejects source changes during capture. `python scripts/check_garage_previews.py` rejects stale sources or altered images before Android export. Rebuild images with the pinned graphical engine and `--path game --script res://../scripts/bake_garage_previews.gd`. No external image generation is used. The final bake incorporates the concurrently corrected electric bonnet without claiming that geometry as part of this task.
+
+The compact recording is presentation/evidence storage only; canonical `DriveFrame`, simulation and input behavior are unchanged by this patch. Launch markers, all four control channels, monotonic input offsets and the 216,000-input cap remain. New `bmt-local-trajectory-v1` journals are local files; the server still receives the existing trajectory contract. Existing replay bytes and hashes are never rewritten. An old trajectory journal without transport options pins its first recovered transport selection for subsequent retries. Legacy input-only migration and accepted-ticket recovery retain their original keys and bodies. The focused upload recovery suite has 44 passing checks.
+
+Faster menu replacement exposed input-release fallthrough into the concurrently added header car picker. The guest transition now runs after the button's input dispatch; its destination also checks that Account still owns navigation. The original tutorial assertions are retained, with its first Garage visit awaiting the new covered preparation. The full 168-check tutorial and 141-check App suite pass. The old folder-concurrency fixture now enters the actual Challenges browser before asserting its unchanged tab/request fences; the previous landing-page mismatch is independently reproduced with task-start scripts. The 72-check graphical retention test passes with identical achievement providers in its production/reference/control rooms. Its initial empty-provider reference omitted the actual trophy wall. No pixel tolerance is changed: retained/fresh differences are four pixels and summed delta 29, exactly the contemporaneous fresh/fresh control; both reflection captures are byte-identical, and six Settings returns preserve the complete main image exactly.
+
+## Support and symbols
+
+Settings > Help > **Copy diagnostic report** is an explicit local clipboard action available to guests and opted-out players. It contains build/source identity, engine/platform/renderer, bounded device/OS descriptions and up to four recent Android crash/ANR records. The final report is at most 16 KiB. Android traces are read only on that action, at most 256 KiB per trace, with at most 24 validated first-party frames per exit. Native protobuf parsing selects the crashing thread when its ID is available. Raw logs, abort messages, memory/register dumps, process IDs, paths, account fields, credentials, tracks and recordings are discarded. Missing, rotated, malformed or unavailable OS traces produce an otherwise useful report without frames.
+
+Backend logs add `bmt_backend.module:function:line` (or `external`) beside the existing request ID and exception type. They do not add exception text, locals or submitted bodies. The quality dashboard explicitly distinguishes this local support route from its existing signed-in, consented telemetry; it continues to report automatic guest/crash-stack/Play-vitals ingestion as unavailable.
+
+`build_track_geometry.ps1` now compiles debug information, extracts separate debug files, strips the packaged library and writes `build/symbols/<packaged-binary-sha256>/mapping.json`. Keep that directory privately with each release's build identity, source checkpoint, APK/AAB hash, native ELF build IDs and any Java obfuscation mapping. The disposable Windows symbol fixture proves actual address-to-source resolution; production libraries were not rebuilt in this task. Obtain the **matching** official Godot Android template symbols, or symbols from the identical custom template build, following [Godot's symbol guidance](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/platform/android/resolving_crashes_on_android.html).
+
+For a player report, identify its build and matching release artifact first, resolve retained relative PCs against the matching library/symbols, and correlate backend request IDs with safe failure sites. Review Play Console Android vitals after each rollout and regularly thereafter; group crashes/ANRs by build, OS/device, frequency and affected users, resolve native symbols, and track each reproduced regression to a verification build. Record the review window and provider outage explicitly. This is an operator workflow, not a newly connected feed. Android's [exit-info reference](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ApplicationExitInfo#getTraceInputStream()) documents nullable/rotated traces and native protobuf tombstones from API 31; the [AOSP schema](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/refs/heads/main/debuggerd/proto/tombstone.proto) defines the fields read by the bounded parser.
+
+## Verification and remaining acceptance
+
+Use [report.json](evidence/mobile-audit-fixes-2026-10-26/report.json) for exact commands, exit status, durations, source hashes, initial failures and scoped review patch. [The evidence folder](evidence/mobile-audit-fixes-2026-10-26/) includes native Store/Garage/Help captures and raw logs. All native commands use `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` with isolated save/session/cache paths and no configured live API. Desktop Mobile means Vulkan on this workstation, not an attached device.
+
+Passing checks include focused storage/cache/lifetime/support tests (263 Compatibility and 261 desktop Mobile before the final two image-content assertions), Store 131/144/144, Garage Parts configurator 600 headless/647 Compatibility, native reflections 25, App 141, tutorial 168, upload recovery 44, background scalability 18, launch 18,656, driving 72, rewind 61, graphics settings 146, client quality 57, localization 62 and packaged translations 302. Backend quality/network/failure-site tests pass 32 tests as reported by pytest. Final parser/import and Java/Python checks are recorded separately.
+
+Retained failures are not counted as passes. Editor practice reproduces the same four failures and subsequent Nil-state error with task-start scripts. Broader historical replay/recovery and exact old-handling suites contain separate contract/fixture failures; their original and isolated task-start results are retained in the report. Some native Store/reflection test exits report four leaked objects and one retained resource; the focused lifecycle/cache runs do not. The sandbox's certificate-store error remains an environmental limitation. None of these logs is silently classified as error-free.
+
+Reload/rebuild the client to use the changes; deploy backend logging/coverage changes only through the separately authorized service rollout. Device startup/Garage latency, touch/appearance, deliberate disposable Android crash/ANR collection, matching production symbols and operational Play-vitals access still require acceptance. No device attachment check/test, APK/AAB build, real authentication/purchase, live data mutation, deployment, merge, owner-process restart or commit was performed. Concurrent header, Garage, electric, handling, track and Rivalry changes are preserved and excluded from the task-only patch.
